From 8225f3fb0fadde8f64fc68234ed2837a098a77af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shibco <cade@parare.al>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:58:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 95/95] winex11: improve scrolling inertia and middle-drag
 throw

Keep direct fine scrolling and middle-button navigation enabled. Enable
inertia and throw by default, with a separate switch for each.

Start fine-scroll inertia after an end report or after 100 ms without a new
report. Judge a middle-drag throw from its latest moving release, including
coalesced movement reports.

Use a slower default decay of 3.0. Limit each continued message to 15 units,
each axis to 480 units, the total to 960 units and each run to 224 messages.
Do not replay missed movement after a pause.

Keep normal wheel clicks working while a user holds a button, except during
middle-button navigation. Continue to block smooth scrolling, pinch and
delayed movement during a drag.

Accept named values without regard to case. Treat off and 0 as disabled where
supported. Report invalid values in the normal log.

Initialise timing once and turn continued movement off if setup fails. Keep at
most one waiting update for each movement. Stop it when its input or window
changes.
